t-we-do/workplace-and-skills/employment-permits/permit-types/critical-skills-employment-permit/","title":"Department of Enterprise, Tourism and Employment, Critical Skills Employment Permit: €40,904, €36,848, €68,911, public sector pay agreements, 2-year job offer, 50% rule, immediate family reunification","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-09"},{"id":"frp-nuclear-family","url":"https://www.irishimmigration.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Family-Reunification-Policy-12-June-2026.pdf","title":"Policy Document on Non-EEA Family Reunification (12 June 2026), paras. 1.5.1, 6.3 and 10.8: a Critical Skills Employment Permit holder''s spouse, partner and minor children may come on arrival","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"frp-spouse","url":"https://www.irishimmigration.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Family-Reunification-Policy-12-June-2026.pdf","title":"Family Reunification Policy, paras. 7.5 and 7.10: a spouse or civil partner must be 18 or over at application; a recognised civil partnership counts as marriage","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"frp-de-facto-partner","url":"https://www.irishimmigration.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Family-Reunification-Policy-12-June-2026.pdf","title":"Family Reunification Policy, glossary and paras. 7.12 to 7.13: a de facto partner 18 or over, in a relationship akin to marriage with at least 2 years of cohabitation before applying","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"frp-children","url":"https://www.irishimmigration.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Family-Reunification-Policy-12-June-2026.pdf","title":"Family Reunification Policy, paras. 7.21, 7.22, 7.24, 7.26 and 8.2: biological, adopted or step-children, unmarried and under 18; stepchildren must be full-time members of the household","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"isd-family-reunification-june-2026","url":"https://www.irishimmigration.ie/amendments-to-policy-on-non-eea-family-reunification/","title":"Immigration Service Delivery: amendments to the non-EEA Family Reunification Policy take effect from 12 June 2026","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"age-of-majority-act","url":"https://www.irishstatutebook.ie/eli/1985/act/2/section/4/enacted/en/html","title":"Age of Majority Act 1985, s. 4(1): an age is attained at the start of the birthday anniversary; no Irish rule for a 29 February birthday was found, so 28 February is assumed","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-07"},{"id":"ep-regs-fees","url":"https://www.irishstatutebook.ie/eli/2024/si/444/made/en/html","title":"S.I. No. 444 of 2024, reg. 7, Schedule 1: €1,000 for a critical skills employment permit; no fee for a registered charity or an EEA, Swiss or UK national''s spouse or civil partner; 90% back on refusal","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-09"},{"id":"dete-fees","url":"https://enterprise.gov.ie/en/what-we-do/workplace-and-skills/employment-permits/fees/","title":"Department of Enterprise, Tourism and Employment, Fees for Employment Permits: €1,000 for a Critical Skills Employment Permit of up to 24 months","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-09"}],"countries":{"id":"countries","number":1},"formerCountries":{"id":"former-countries","number":1},"officialDomains":[{"id":"ie","number":1}],"countrySets":[{"id":"eu-free-movement","number":1}],"requirements":[{"id":"not-eu-eea-swiss-or-british-citizen","title":"Not a citizen of Ireland, another EU or EEA state, Switzerland or the United Kingdom: they work in Ireland without an employment permit","expression":{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"not","operand":{"op":"intersects","list":{"op":"fact","key":"principal.citizenships"},"set":{"op":"set","id":"eu-free-movement"}}},{"op":"not","operand":{"op":"intersects","list":{"op":"fact","key":"principal.citizenships"},"set":{"op":"tokens","values":["GB"]}}}]},"sources":["ep-act-foreign-national","ep-act-eu-treaty-rights","immigration-act-1999-non-national","aliens-exemption-order-1999","dete-who-needs-a-